    <summary>Fast HTTP(S) debugging proxy to intercept, inspect, mock and replay traffic.</summary>
    <description><![CDATA[Akev is an open-source HTTP(S) debugging proxy for developers, testers and security engineers. Launch a browser, terminal, Android device or container with one click and every request it makes shows up as it happens: headers, bodies, timings, TLS details and the app that sent it. Then change anything: mock responses, rewrite requests, map to local files, throttle the network or pause at breakpoints.

## Features

- One-click interception for Chrome, Edge, Firefox and other browsers, new terminals, Android over ADB, Docker, Electron apps and the system proxy
- HTTP/1.1, HTTP/2, WebSockets, SSE, gRPC and protobuf, with optional HTTP/3 over QUIC
- Rules that mock, rewrite, map, delay, throttle or block traffic, with live hit counters
- Compose and replay requests, and export them as code for 20 languages
- Import HAR, Charles, mitmproxy and Fiddler (.saz) captures
- `akev capture -- <command>` runs tests through the proxy and writes a HAR, for CI
- A built-in MCP server lets AI coding agents search captured traffic, with secrets redacted
- No account and no telemetry

Mocking, rewriting, breakpoints and HAR import and export are free. Akev Pro (a one-time licence) adds scripting, TLS fingerprint impersonation, WireGuard capture, transparent capture, JVM attach, protobuf schemas and an LLM traffic view; licence keys are checked offline.

## Notes

- This package installs the desktop app (MSI, all users). The x64 build is used on x64 Windows and the arm64 build on Windows on Arm.
- The app updates itself after you confirm; `choco upgrade akev` works too.
]]></description>
    <releaseNotes>https://github.com/akevdev/akev/releases/tag/v0.1.0</releaseNotes>
  </metadata>
